course: dictionary
lesson: 12218
title: Connected: joined, linked and related
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Connected means joined or linked to something else. Look at the words around it to find the meaning. «The two rooms are connected by a door.» The door joins the rooms, so connected means joined together.
explain: Connected can also mean related, so one thing has something to do with another. «The clues in the story are connected to the crime.» The clues are not joined to the crime by string. They have something to do with it. Ask yourself: is one thing joined to another, or does it have something to do with it?
explain: Connected is also the past form of the verb connect. «Ben connected the lamp to the plug.» Here Ben did the joining in the past. Connect, connects and connecting are the other forms, so you can spot the same word in different shapes.
fact: Connected means joined or linked to something else.
fact: Connected can mean related, so that one thing has something to do with another.
fact: Connected can mean linked to the internet, a network or a phone line.
fact: «Connected» is the past form of «connect».
fact: Phrases you may meet include connected to, connected with, well connected and stay connected.
exercise: «The two rooms are connected by a door.» What does connected mean here? | *Joined or linked to each other | Empty and quiet | Painted in bright colours | Hidden away from view
exercise: «The clues in the story are connected to the crime.» What does connected mean here? | Happy and smiling | *Related, with something to do with the crime | Cold and wet | Put away in a box
exercise: «Ben connected the lamp to the plug.» Find and copy the word that shows the past form of connect. | Ben | lamp | plug | *connected
test: «My tablet is connected to the wi-fi.» What does connected mean? | Cut into small pieces | *Linked to the internet | Dropped on the floor with a bang | Sad and lonely
test: «They stay connected with their cousins, even across the sea.» What does stay connected suggest? | Stay in bed all day | Never speak to them again | *Keep in touch and feel close | Forget their names
exam: «In science, a circuit works only when all the parts are connected.» What must the parts be? | Hidden in a box | *Joined so the electricity can flow | Painted in bright colours | Far apart from each other
